## 4. Logs — ECS-style fields for ELK / OpenSearch

Use **ECS** (Elastic Common Schema) where possible so Kibana default dashboards and cross-team queries work.

### 4.1 Core ECS (every log line should try to have)

| ECS field | Your content |
|-----------|----------------|
| `@timestamp` | Event time (UTC). |
| `message` | Human line (optional if JSON-only). |
| `log.level` | `info`, `warn`, `error`. |
| `service.name` | Same as Prometheus `service`. |
| `service.version` | Image tag / git short sha. |
| `service.environment` | `dev` / `staging` / `prod`. |
| `cloud.region` | If applicable. |
| `trace.id` | W3C trace id (hex). |
| `span.id` | Current span id. |
| `transaction.id` | Optional business transaction. |
| `error.type`, `error.message`, `error.stack_trace` | On failures. |

### 4.2 **Custom namespace** for LLM (prefix avoids ECS collisions)

Use a single prefix: **`llm.`** nested object or flat keys with `llm_` prefix (pick one style per index and stick to it).

| Field | Type | Notes |
|-------|------|--------|
| `llm.module` | keyword | e.g. `voice.sentiment` |
| `llm.function` | keyword | Callable / operation name |
| `llm.model_id` | keyword | Provider model string |
| `llm.flow_id` | keyword | **OK in logs** (high cardinality acceptable in logs, not in metric labels) |
| `llm.pass_index` | byte | 1 or 2 for dual audio pass |
| `llm.tokens.input` | long | |
| `llm.tokens.output` | long | |
| `llm.tokens.thinking` | long | nullable |
| `llm.estimated_cost_usd` | double | |
| `llm.rate_card_version` | keyword | e.g. `2026-04-20` |
| `llm.attempt` | byte | Retry attempt |
| `llm.retry_reason` | keyword | `429`, `timeout`, `parser_failed` |
| `llm.hard_reset` | boolean | |
| `llm.structured_parse_ok` | boolean | |
| `llm.outcome` | keyword | `success`, `parser_failed`, `retry_exhausted` |
| `llm.latency_ms` | long | |
| `event.dataset` | keyword | e.g. `llm.invocation` — for ILM / dashboard filters |

**PII:** Prefer `audio.content_sha256`, `audio.duration_sec`, not raw audio in logs unless approved.

